  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Onboarding Stepper Flow\n\nA multi-step onboarding scene: a stepper advances across three panels (an input, a radio, a switch) while the Next button presses, and the last press runs the Finish button to success.\n\nCategory: ui-blocks. Length: 5.85 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Demoing a multi-step onboarding experience (account setup, plan choice, preferences) in one scene.\n- Showing progressive form completion with a stepper indicator advancing across panels.\n- A product video needs a complete new-user flow from first input to success without custom orchestration.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The flow is a payment checkout: use checkout-flow.\n- It is a single account sign-up (email and password, then success): use signup-flow.\n- You need custom panel content like images or code blocks: the panels are fixed, so orchestrate manually.\n\nVariables:\n- steps (string): Steps, default \"[\\\"Account\\\", \\\"Plan\\\", \\\"Settings\\\"]\"\n- name (string): Name, default \"jane@acme.com\"\n- plans (string): Plans, default \"[\\\"Free\\\", \\\"Pro\\\", \\\"Team\\\"]\"\n- next_label (string): Next label, default \"Next\"\n- finish_label (string): Finish label, default \"Finish\"\n- mode (enum): Mode, default \"light\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n- transparent (boolean): Transparent, default false\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
